  "markdown": "9. Which one of the following will most readily be dehydrated in acidic condition?\n\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">a) \n\n<description>The figure shows a chemical structure, 4-hydroxypentan-2-one, represented in skeletal formula. It consists of a five-carbon chain. A carbonyl group (C=O) is located at the second carbon position, and a hydroxyl group (-OH) is attached to the fourth carbon position. The structure is drawn with standard skeletal bond lines.</description></figure>\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">b) \n\n<description>A skeletal structure of 2-pentanol. The molecule consists of a five-carbon chain with a hydroxyl group (-OH) attached to the second carbon atom.</description></figure>\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">c) \n\n<description>The image displays a chemical structure labeled 'c)'. The structure is a hydroxy ketone, specifically 3-hydroxybutan-2-one (or similar depending on chain length). It consists of a four-carbon chain with a carbonyl group (C=O) at the second position and a hydroxyl group (-OH) attached to the third carbon. Specifically, it features a terminal methyl group on the left, a carbonyl group, a central CH group with an -OH substituent, and a terminal methyl group on the right (part of an ethyl chain). The bond lines are standard skeletal structure representation.</description></figure>\n\n<figure type=\"DIAGRAM\">d) \n\n<description>The figure shows a chemical structure diagram representing 2-pentanone. The molecule consists of a five-carbon chain. A carbonyl group (C=O) is attached to the second carbon atom. The structure starts with a methyl group on the left, followed by a ketone functional group, and continues with a propyl chain (three carbons) extending to the right.</description></figure>\n\n10. *Tert*-butyl methyl ether on heating with anhydrous HI in ether gives\na) CH<sub>3</sub>OH + (CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>Cl b) CH<sub>3</sub>I + (CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>COH c) CH<sub>3</sub>I + (CH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>Cl d) 